%% 14-runbooks-incident — memory pressure on a 7.6 GiB box.
%% Source of truth: src/14-runbooks-incident.mmd. Generated outputs are never hand-edited.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% atlas-participant K uptime-kuma
    participant K as uptime-kuma
    %% atlas-participant T telegram
    participant T as Telegram
    %% atlas-participant Y debian
    participant Y as User
    %% atlas-participant E linux
    participant E as earlyoom
    %% atlas-participant C docker
    participant C as containers

    Note over K,C: 7.6 GiB RAM,<br/>swap can run close to capacity.
    C-->>E: memory climbs
    alt earlyoom fires first
        E->>C: kill the largest offender
        K->>T: service down alert
    else probe fails first
        K->>T: service down alert
    end
    T->>Y: notification
    Y->>C: docker stats — find the offender
    Note over Y,C: do NOT stop a container to free memory.<br/>Prefer cpu-shares / renice first.<br/>Preserve stateful job queues.
    alt a heavy job is running
        Y->>C: renice / lower cpu-shares
    else genuinely stuck
        Y->>Y: get explicit OK before stopping anything
        Y->>C: stop the single offender only
    end
    Y->>K: confirm probes green again
    Note over Y: record it in the workspace —<br/>operations log is the running log
